{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"41e51e2ba7fd1f89ef55aa1d30bdebcb50bf5d5995874f7a7717cd7a6911427e","digest":{"component_or_area":"schemas drift gate","key_entities":["docs/adr/0004","_engine/rebar_reconciler/_snapshot_schema.py","fetcher.py","src/rebar/schemas/","schemas.load()","jsonschema","Draft202012Validator","python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types","_build-and-test.yml:545","bridge_state/snapshots/","tests/fixtures/jira/"],"problem_keywords":["snapshot-entry contract","schema enforcement","drift detection","schema drift gate","contract validation"],"propositions":["The snapshot-entry schema contract in _snapshot_schema.py is not enforced because fetcher.py never imports it and no production module depends on it.","The snapshot-entry schema should be moved from a hand-rolled Python module outside src/rebar/schemas/ into the tracked schemas directory where 90 sibling schemas are automatically validated via jsonschema and a CI drift gate.","A redacted fixture covering populated, parent-absent, and empty snapshot shapes must be derived from real fetcher output in bridge_state/snapshots/ and placed in tests/fixtures/jira/.","The generated-types drift gate (python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types at _build-and-test.yml:545) must validate the snapshot-entry contract alongside existing schemas to catch field changes that diverge from the contract."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787896875675415001,"uuid":"32f7b8b8-dfeb-4910-816b-2772b19ee70b"}